1
00:01:30,840 --> 00:02:00,820
Oh, my God.

2
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:03,760
Oh, thank you, Kodaka. That was really nice of you.

3
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:05,660
Now, if you'll excuse me...

4
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,000
You know what? Hold on a sec.

5
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,640
Let me get one.

6
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,440
I appreciate that, Kodaka.

7
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:11,600
You're very welcome, Aoi.

8
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:14,560
I guess you can go ahead and follow me this way if you want to.

9
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,540
Carrying two boxes this heavy at once

10
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,340
makes it seem like you want them to fall.

11
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:23,160
I don't.

12
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:25,740
I'm just trying to make up time on my student council work

13
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,980
since I skipped it for a week.

14
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:28,280
You skipped for a week?

15
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:34,480
Hey, do you mind telling me

16
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,800
why you were so set on destroying the Neighbors Club?

17
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:40,120
Because Senna is exceptionally gifted,

18
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,560
and she should be somewhere appropriate for her gifts.

19
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,700
What do you mean, somewhere appropriate?

20
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:47,900
Face it. Senna Kashiwazaki is unbelievably talented

21
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:49,880
and needed a better way to make use of those talents.

22
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,860
Your club was just a waste of her time.

23
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:52,420
Wow.

24
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:55,120
So then, you tried to disband the Neighbors Club

25
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,960
for the sake of your so-called mortal enemy?

26
00:02:57,020 --> 00:02:57,340
Yes.

27
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,220
If you say so.

28
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:05,020
I guess she has a point.

29
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:08,360
Senna would be an asset to any club she decided to join.

30
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:10,340
It's not just her, either.

31
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:13,940
Yozara and Rika have that super smart thing going on for them.

32
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:16,020
And then you have Yukimura and Kobito,

33
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:17,080
who are both popular.

34
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:18,980
Maybe Aoi's right.

35
00:03:18,980 --> 00:03:21,780
Maybe there's really no point to even having the Neighbors Club.

36
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,100
Oh, I'm just kidding.

37
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:23,820
You what?

38
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:25,360
I don't like Senna.

39
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:27,260
She gets everything her little heart desires,

40
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:28,540
so I just wanted her to realize

41
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:30,040
she might lose something one day.

42
00:03:30,340 --> 00:03:32,880
So, in other words, I'm wicked jealous of her.

43
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:34,920
Well, the funny thing is, you're wrong.

44
00:03:35,020 --> 00:03:36,000
She doesn't have everything.

45
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:36,520
Yeah?

46
00:03:36,980 --> 00:03:38,240
What doesn't she have?

47
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:39,360
She doesn't have friends.

48
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:41,860
Jeez, are you okay?

49
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:46,680
Why are you laughing?

50
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:49,700
I forgot you have such a great sense of humor.

51
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:51,400
You're hilarious, you know that?

52
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:52,900
I'm not falling for it, though.

53
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:54,820
There's not a single person in the whole world

54
00:03:54,820 --> 00:03:55,900
who doesn't have friends.

55
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:57,860
I wouldn't be so sure.

56
00:03:58,340 --> 00:03:59,800
It was really sweet of you

57
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,740
to try and cheer me up after what I did.

58
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:03,000
Thank you again, Kodaka.

59
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:03,760
Huh?

60
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,660
Almost there.

61
00:04:12,720 --> 00:04:13,840
You were a big help.

62
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,140
I couldn't have done it without you.

63
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:16,580
You still have more, yeah?

64
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:17,840
I can help you with those.

65
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,780
No, I can't ask you to do that.

66
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:21,440
This stuff got piled up

67
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:22,520
because of the neighbor's club.

68
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,120
So I'm partly to blame.

69
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,280
I can't not help you.

70
00:04:25,860 --> 00:04:28,020
Don't you need to go meet with that club, though?

71
00:04:28,380 --> 00:04:29,640
Well, we're not really big

72
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,200
on planning activities every day.

73
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,980
So if we have other stuff to do first,

74
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:33,820
it's not a big deal.

75
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:37,120
Why do I feel like I have to make excuses?

76
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,260
Weird.

77
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:44,640
Well, on the bright side, we made it halfway.

78
00:04:44,860 --> 00:04:45,680
I guess so.

79
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,920
Well, you two seem to be working well together.

80
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:52,640
Hinata, what did you come out here for?

81
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:54,620
I heard some extremely nice individuals

82
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:55,940
started helping you with your chores.

83
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:58,440
I thought I'd come check on you and thank him myself.

84
00:04:58,520 --> 00:04:59,800
Oh, uh, hello.

85
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:02,320
I'm Kodaka Hasegawa from Class 2-5.

86
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,160
Oh, yeah.

87
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:04,560
Yeah, it's totally you.

88
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:06,080
Wait, you know who he is?

89
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,380
Nope, no clue.

90
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,860
Then what the heck was that reaction about?

91
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:10,520
I don't know.

92
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:11,340
Call it a whim.

93
00:05:13,480 --> 00:05:15,500
I'm Hinata, the student council president.

94
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:16,900
It's nice to meet you.

95
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,460
Yeah, cool.

96
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:31,960
Hey, I was wondering, why are you helping Aoi?

97
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,120
This is a lot of work.

98
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:35,660
You guys must be, like, dating or something, yeah?

99
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:37,240
No, we're not dating.

100
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:39,680
Besides, Kodaka probably already has a girlfriend.

101
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:41,340
Do you have a girlfriend?

102
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:42,060
Um, no.

103
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:43,700
Come on, you're telling me

104
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:45,840
that you're not dating anyone from the neighbor's club?

105
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,600
No, I am not.

106
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,640
It just isn't like that with them, okay?

107
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,140
Hmm, probably for the best.

108
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:53,040
What do you mean?

109
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,360
What's for the best?

110
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,080
Well, if you think about it,

111
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,500
you're the only boy in the whole club,

112
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:58,920
so you're surrounded by girls.

113
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:00,300
If you dated one of them,

114
00:06:00,380 --> 00:06:01,680
the whole atmosphere would get,

115
00:06:02,140 --> 00:06:03,920
like, way awkward.

116
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:06,260
Yeah, that's for sure.

117
00:06:07,020 --> 00:06:08,800
So, if you're not her boyfriend,

118
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:10,080
why are you helping out?

119
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,900
Because he happens to be one of those guys

120
00:06:11,900 --> 00:06:12,940
who comes to the rescue

121
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:14,220
when he sees someone in trouble.

122
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:15,040
Oh, my.

123
00:06:15,260 --> 00:06:16,660
Well, isn't that fancy?

124
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:20,860
Keep up the good work, kid.

125
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:24,840
Okay, I think that's it.

126
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:29,260
For the last time,

127
00:06:29,340 --> 00:06:30,720
thanks so much for your help.

128
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:31,800
Don't worry about it.

129
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:32,700
It's not a problem.

130
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:33,580
See you later.

131
00:06:34,900 --> 00:06:36,400
Oh, hey, uh, Kodaka.

132
00:06:36,780 --> 00:06:37,000
Yeah?

133
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,840
You seem like you're a cool guy.

134
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:41,040
Want to join the student council with us?

135
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:41,360
Huh?

136
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,580
We just lost our general affairs person,

137
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,860
so we're looking for a replacement,

138
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:46,000
if you're interested.

139
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:47,860
You should definitely join.

140
00:06:47,940 --> 00:06:49,300
It'll be a ton of fun, I promise.

141
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:49,900
Really?

142
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:51,620
I'm surprised you'd want to work with me.

143
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:54,120
Actually, the council only has girls on it right now.

144
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:56,400
I think it would be nice for us to have a guy around.

145
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:57,520
Honestly, Kodaka,

146
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,480
you would be perfect on the student council.

147
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:00,680
I don't know.

148
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:03,380
Haven't you heard the way people talk about me?

149
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:05,200
I don't want to bring you guys down.

150
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:06,700
I don't get it.

151
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:08,520
What's wrong with this super cool

152
00:07:08,520 --> 00:07:10,200
bad boy chic real life haver?

153
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:11,720
Yeah, thank you,

154
00:07:11,780 --> 00:07:13,720
but you're the only one who thinks that about me.

155
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:14,080
You're welcome.

156
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:16,000
See, most people don't think I'm bad boy chic.

157
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,220
They assume I'm just bad.

158
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:19,760
I get called a delinquent and all sorts of mean things.

159
00:07:19,920 --> 00:07:21,920
It's because I have weird hair and a grumpy face.

160
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:25,640
That's true.

161
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,300
Your hair does get attention,

162
00:07:27,460 --> 00:07:28,840
and you have evil-looking eyes.

163
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,180
There, you see?

164
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:31,860
Putting me on the student council

165
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:32,900
would wreck your reputation,

166
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:33,900
and I don't want to do that.

167
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,420
Only fools judge on appearances,

168
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:37,560
and I simply don't care what fools think.

169
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:39,760
Are you going to let idiots decide

170
00:07:39,760 --> 00:07:40,940
what you can and can't do?

171
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,480
What's the matter, Kodika?

172
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,680
You look a little dazed.

173
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:47,460
No, I mean, yes, I'm fine.

174
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:48,660
Good to hear.

175
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,180
So, are you going to join?

176
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,620
No, no, I'm sorry.

177
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,160
I think the student council

178
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:56,700
might be a little too much for me.

179
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:58,860
But if all you need is more manual labor,

180
00:07:58,960 --> 00:07:59,620
just let me know.

181
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:00,700
I'd be happy to help out

182
00:08:00,700 --> 00:08:02,140
whenever and wherever I can.

183
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,960
Plus, I'm almost always free.

184
00:08:03,960 --> 00:08:04,320
Really?

185
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:05,800
The library asked for us

186
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:06,680
to help with a project,

187
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,080
so if you'd like to come by tomorrow,

188
00:08:08,180 --> 00:08:09,160
that would be so great.

189
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:09,520
Sure.

190
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:10,820
Count on me to be there.

191
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:11,020
Mm-hmm.

192
00:08:11,540 --> 00:08:12,740
That's a perfect answer.

193
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:15,720
A week went by so fast,

194
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:16,980
I barely even realized

195
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:17,760
what was happening.

196
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:20,860
I ended up helping the student council

197
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:21,860
pretty much every day.

198
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:23,880
It's kind of funny.

199
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,900
All the kids at school

200
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,380
think Hinata is like a god

201
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:28,860
for getting that punk in line.

202
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:29,220
Just a second.

203
00:08:29,640 --> 00:08:30,400
Don't forget to sweat every day.

204
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:32,380
She's getting even more popular than before.

205
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:35,640
My reputation's the same, though.

206
00:08:35,640 --> 00:08:35,960
Holy crap, I'm sorry!

207
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,120
No surprise there.

208
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:39,560
I haven't set foot

209
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,000
into our club room since then.

210
00:08:41,420 --> 00:08:42,300
Don't get me wrong,

211
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:42,940
the neighbor's club

212
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,120
still means a lot to me.

213
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:46,400
But after running out on them like that,

214
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:47,660
I couldn't go back.

215
00:08:48,140 --> 00:08:49,280
I don't know why.

216
00:08:49,780 --> 00:08:50,600
I just couldn't.

217
00:08:57,080 --> 00:08:58,760
Look who I finally found.

218
00:08:58,760 --> 00:08:58,820
Oh.

219
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:05,140
Yuki Mura.

220
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:08,100
Big brother.

221
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:15,340
Oh.

222
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:16,580
Hey, Yuki Mura.

223
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:17,680
What's up?

224
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:20,240
I heard a despicable gang captured you

225
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,460
and that they were forcing you

226
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,560
to do manual labor.

227
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,120
So I have come to your rescue.

228
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:25,900
You know, that's really rude to say.

229
00:09:26,180 --> 00:09:27,880
Kodaka's helping us because he's nice

230
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,120
and that's all there is to it.

231
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,240
Seriously?

232
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:31,560
Is that the truth, brother?

233
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:32,760
Yeah.

234
00:09:33,320 --> 00:09:34,060
In that case,

235
00:09:34,140 --> 00:09:35,180
I shall help out as well.

236
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:36,300
No thanks.

237
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:37,340
And besides,

238
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:38,340
why would you?

239
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,000
Aren't you the one

240
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,060
who wanted to poison me?

241
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:40,640
I am.

242
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:41,860
Why are you wearing

243
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,060
a boy's uniform anyway?

244
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,200
I'm wearing this uniform

245
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,220
because I'm endeavoring

246
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:46,200
to become a true man.

247
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,580
You want to be a true man?

248
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:48,780
What does that even mean?

249
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:50,720
It means I want to be a great man.

250
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:51,200
What?

251
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:52,720
You do realize

252
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,800
you're a girl, don't you?

253
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:55,340
That is of no importance.

254
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:56,780
True and genuine men

255
00:09:56,780 --> 00:09:58,300
can transcend their birth gender.

256
00:09:58,500 --> 00:09:58,740
Huh?

257
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,260
Have you just been let out

258
00:10:00,260 --> 00:10:01,220
of an insane asylum?

259
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,820
Because you sound kind of crazy.

260
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:04,760
Big brother,

261
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:06,740
may I slay that villain, please?

262
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:07,560
You may not slay

263
00:10:07,560 --> 00:10:08,620
student council members.

264
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:09,820
I'm sorry, Aoi,

265
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:10,940
but will you excuse us

266
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:11,380
for a minute?

267
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:11,900
Sure.

268
00:10:12,180 --> 00:10:13,580
If that's what you really want.

269
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:15,980
So tell me,

270
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:17,360
anything new

271
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:18,220
at the neighbor's club?

272
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:18,940
No.

273
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:21,180
Senna is still totally engrossed

274
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:22,100
with those video games

275
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:22,900
about making friends

276
00:10:22,900 --> 00:10:23,860
with girls and stuff.

277
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,280
Man, she just won't give up

278
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,160
on those, will she?

279
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:27,660
How is everyone else doing?

280
00:10:27,960 --> 00:10:28,740
I'm not sure.

281
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:29,960
Yozra and Rika

282
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,020
haven't been to the clubroom

